			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule — Formatting pass and documentation cleanup\n\nUpdate the Element submodule pointer to ff6473f0, which incorporates two commits formatting Air, Common, Grove, Maintain, Mountain, Vine, Worker, and Wind while removing deprecated architecture references from documentation.\n\n**Air** (style/docs): Add blank lines for visual separation in control flow blocks across 25 Rust source files. Remove deprecated `Plugins` and `Mountain` module references from README.\n\n**Common** (style/docs): Insert empty lines between variable declarations in LanguageFeature providers and telemetry modules. Refactor transport layer documentation to reflect trait-based `TransportStrategy` abstraction.\n\n**Grove** (docs): Remove deprecated `Source/API/`, `Source/Common/`, `Source/Services/`, and `Proto/Grove.proto` references. Update sequence diagrams to specify \"gRPC via Vine\" instead of Grove-specific protocols.\n\n**Maintain** (style): Add blank lines between struct fields and module declarations in Eliminate transform CLI components.\n\n**Mountain** (refactor): Normalize import separation between canonical library imports and local `crate::` bindings. Remove dead code including unused `TlsCommands`, `EmitWithTraceparent`, and dormant RPC dispatch arms.\n\n**Vine** (docs): Remove dead Grove references from architecture documentation. Simplify Mermaid diagram to show only production gRPC topology: Mountain ↔ Cocoon and Mountain ↔ Air.\n\n**Worker** (style): Apply consistent formatting across ESBuild configuration and Service Worker source files.\n\n**Wind** (style): Add consistent whitespace across logging and telemetry modules (Trace.ts, PostHogBridge.ts, Sandbox.ts, Tier.ts, WorkbenchIntegrationImplementation.ts). Enhance error handling in Trace.ts.\n\nAll changes are cosmetic or documentation updates with no functional behavior changes except Mountain's removal of dormant RPC arms.",
